{"id": "clm:458c382a868f36303caf4018afa93509178007dcaf3aa8df745d80434097fcb7", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas database users are separate from Atlas application users. Management roles govern Atlas UI/API actions, while database roles determine access when clients connect to clusters. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-users.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Access Control and RBAC"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/auth/authorization.md", "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/opensource/decoupling-authorization-at-scale-mongodb-atlas-and-cedar-based-resource-policies/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d14844f576bda1c75c9d2e6b829a93f8add9acb4a2ee0d091b84686caded26aa", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:70d2fd9f3298a1035ff9c305bf1254ca64021548d8ca0cdca394353bb3be2ebe", "ev:d7f0cc1411e0daacc392998ec477b0c006d95a74fecea897ba8efc21dae389b6"]}
{"id": "clm:3b2c20192d5038befe5c018bd347c9bb0580194af23f494e98bd1e4bc0b5ca1b", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas recommends assigning the minimum required permissions and using fine-grained custom database roles when predefined privileges are too broad; those roles can scope actions to particular databases and collections. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/auth/authorization.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Access Control and RBAC"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-roles.md", "https://docs.atlan.com/apps/connectors/database/mongodb/how-tos/set-up-mongodb"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d14844f576bda1c75c9d2e6b829a93f8add9acb4a2ee0d091b84686caded26aa", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4721d30b2372273585c2ebac7a941a52b8767b1098f23af285ed0e079018f727", "ev:7554e277367787b56fe1e2d318fe2173b010961d11c5857c0fe1adcb86ed3aff", "ev:98785064cf32d2c8f3569f99ca6b09571bc06621eff5531cd667ef8a1c1efdce"]}
{"id": "clm:250e5e6f42890e69274fbfcdc1f2713745f0b86383a39f6f8eaa81687771065c", "type": "statement", "text": "An Atlas custom role that grants insert can permit collection creation even when CREATE_COLLECTION is absent. A Terraform report reproduced this behavior, and the MongoDB privilege reference lists create among commands authorized by insert. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/issues/1963", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Access Control and RBAC"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/privilege-actions/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d14844f576bda1c75c9d2e6b829a93f8add9acb4a2ee0d091b84686caded26aa", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:180acc1f2ebe1faa8caf49d46f1af7a9925015036934cab95a9a34c737db8410", "ev:9c5aae69702e41d7e79d1f224a5ac304e7fba0e7ce2cac8537a023a1597dda77"]}
{"id": "clm:2d517fdc3a115c2b19ab7b0a569a7b34ec86feb8186a18af3c28a1b8388fe8ab", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas custom-role actions cover a subset of the actions available to built-in roles; a custom role cannot be assumed to reproduce every built-in capability. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-roles.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Access Control and RBAC"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d14844f576bda1c75c9d2e6b829a93f8add9acb4a2ee0d091b84686caded26aa", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7d08a2b015dbb3402c7968be229b26b556535035762704ab6565bd22c88a7035"]}
{"id": "clm:defa589d804194dc851c2308d9d4b135dead3feea627100453902663214279f0", "type": "statement", "text": "Database role grants combine: Atlas applies custom roles together with built-in roles and directly assigned privileges, and a more restrictive role does not cancel a higher permission granted by another role. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-roles.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Access Control and RBAC"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-users.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d14844f576bda1c75c9d2e6b829a93f8add9acb4a2ee0d091b84686caded26aa", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4f52249d37396ca1bb09d6efe79575d47900c0d6a49ba72a0c505fe70f198c95", "ev:e28e056ca71b9c3083fa367da08ea46866e4320fba3b5b96ae7f9e4a595a8304"]}
{"id": "clm:dd0a48b5670482fd7014db9590c99dbd66abcb5b648e011976f6ee51439efb35", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas database users can access all clusters and federated database instances in their project by default; administrators can restrict a user to selected instances. Resource scoping must therefore be reviewed separately from role selection. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-users.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Access Control and RBAC"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://docs.atlan.com/apps/connectors/database/mongodb/how-tos/set-up-mongodb", "https://developer.hashicorp.com/vault/api-docs/secret/databases/mongodbatlas"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d14844f576bda1c75c9d2e6b829a93f8add9acb4a2ee0d091b84686caded26aa", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:23dfee10c1a9a116766394746b146d9b604a89df63f4d0d669cbfaa62de1aabf", "ev:71ea98d3660a17849182b7b86a0db10e1c51ca237aec52d73ad0cd82aac3464d"]}
{"id": "clm:e8a4a8741b115489aa05e436457712473f29d196aa77e90ca9d9e7c0adf9cc79", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas requires database users and roles to be managed through the Atlas UI, Atlas CLI, Atlas Administration API, or a supported integration; otherwise Atlas rolls back those modifications. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-users.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Access Control and RBAC"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-roles.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d14844f576bda1c75c9d2e6b829a93f8add9acb4a2ee0d091b84686caded26aa", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2d38bb355f3860b44107ff3a5508c18f7bbcf5c59fcf54c668be2a707c85cdd8", "ev:fea254aed29b57dea79b2ceeb2853a64dbe1a6eb15e9ebef00956c4a6089e035"]}
{"id": "clm:0f493e75a9c319c4fd000968aa97cdff9e98f7ca1db93cc9013b1edbb48a5994", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas supports temporary database users that expire automatically, making time-bounded access possible without leaving permanent database credentials. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/auth/authorization.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Access Control and RBAC"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-users.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d14844f576bda1c75c9d2e6b829a93f8add9acb4a2ee0d091b84686caded26aa", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4c6465cdf20e7eaf57f2690420a866765ac8c1b91017732ba19afadeae105140", "ev:7f1b4ed8c00e51de2847bc613df562a9832b4576db3863d3c801f32e19d42025"]}
{"id": "clm:1d5b306a663675894fc7e1b704eacb9afbeac1223d139d3a6e9a9c1e125b6839", "type": "statement", "text": "In Terraform issue 1522, assigning a custom role against an application database produced HTTP 400 UNSUPPORTED_ROLE. Setting roles.database_name to admin fixed the assignment; the custom role resource still defined the actual database and collection privileges. Maintainers documented this distinction in January 2024. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/issues/1522", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Access Control and RBAC"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d14844f576bda1c75c9d2e6b829a93f8add9acb4a2ee0d091b84686caded26aa", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5ffa3b7accafb183f8fc3238389e38f421de53416c4d288242173646ed56125c", "ev:a75105c6d6e38ffa2fca8e16c73dd75d77ffaf6778aa962ec34647bec3cdfe74", "ev:e9cafe31c0373a1589d015c3b07871861e8a1300a34d2cbc0a246575a9eba8dc"]}
{"id": "clm:54f23a51a0b9bb7925bfac091910cab2ac612f75795b2fc8a45a0f2acbf50760", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlan documents a metadata-crawling custom role using listDatabases, sqlGetSchema, dbStats, listCollections, and collStats. Its JDBC validation also requires find, which its recipe scopes to a nonexistent collection to avoid reading existing collection contents. This is connector-specific guidance, not a universal Atlas requirement. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://docs.atlan.com/apps/connectors/database/mongodb/how-tos/set-up-mongodb", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Access Control and RBAC"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d14844f576bda1c75c9d2e6b829a93f8add9acb4a2ee0d091b84686caded26aa", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:98785064cf32d2c8f3569f99ca6b09571bc06621eff5531cd667ef8a1c1efdce"]}
{"id": "clm:4aa0926f3c058b51efe8cf7829e080f08522782e4d626894c7009457f1c13a93", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas can combine a built-in role, multiple custom roles, and specific privileges for one database user; specific privileges can target individual databases and collections. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-users.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Access Control and RBAC"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-roles.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d14844f576bda1c75c9d2e6b829a93f8add9acb4a2ee0d091b84686caded26aa", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:59fac12e1b8dc354222197551e421e256f7d270388a09a59e1603371799c867f"]}
{"id": "clm:fac16d5c1e784eb5d8dae83e1969981ed08303e65b707646a87f1f95c698b765", "type": "statement", "text": "HashiCorp provides an Atlas-specific Vault database plugin that generates unique, ephemeral database-user credentials from configured roles. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://developer.hashicorp.com/vault/api-docs/secret/databases/mongodbatlas", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Access Control and RBAC"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/hashicorp/vault-plugin-database-mongodbatlas"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d14844f576bda1c75c9d2e6b829a93f8add9acb4a2ee0d091b84686caded26aa", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1ac974524767a3badb1fd3c81d4ea8ac1ee51461f54dcedba8482c16ec69ddfe", "ev:bc86e4d9e097b7d7bfb576fce0e9c0681ab90faced9f16d99600d8d4040ff8d2"]}
{"id": "clm:3c66d08998260d7a793a429a668785249aa2e342145083ffc81b27df79225cb2", "type": "statement", "text": "The Vault Atlas database plugin accepts role assignments and a scopes array in creation statements. If scopes is omitted, the plugin defaults to all scopes, so credential automation must explicitly preserve intended deployment restrictions. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://developer.hashicorp.com/vault/api-docs/secret/databases/mongodbatlas", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Atlas Access Control and RBAC"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-users.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d14844f576bda1c75c9d2e6b829a93f8add9acb4a2ee0d091b84686caded26aa", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ed426ffeb05841042bbe37b7234dcd02a4fb2f404c207d4f68a1e37ab19b6fa5"]}
